  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Find ${f}^{\u2033}(-2)$ if $f(x)=2{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-7.$",
  "worked_solution": "Computing the first derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & ={(2{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-7)}^{\u2032} &  \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2{x}^{2}+2\\cdot 4x-0 \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}+8x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the second derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2033}(x) & ={(6{x}^{2}+8x)}^{\u2032} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 6x+8 \\\\  & =12x+8\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the second derivative at $x=-2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2033}(-2) & =12(-2)+8 \\\\  & =-24+8 \\\\  & =-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
